PathwayData.put("data/grammar_vocabulary/units/L01U2.json",{"strand":"grammar_vocabulary","level":1,"cefr":"A1a","unit":2,"theme":"My Family","essential_question":"Who are the people in my family, and what is special about them?","lessons":[{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS1","title":"This Is My Family: my, your, his, her","objectives":["Students will be able to use my, your, his, her, its, our and their before a noun.","Students will be able to choose his or her correctly for boys/men and girls/women.","I can say \"my brother\", \"her name\" and \"their house\".","I can choose his or her correctly."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام my وyour وhis وher وits وour وtheir قبل الاسم.","سيتمكن الطلاب من اختيار his أو her بشكل صحيح.","أستطيع أن أقول my brother وher name وtheir house.","أستطيع أن أختار his أو her بشكل صحيح."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"family","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈfæməli/","definition":"a group of people: parents, children, grandparents and more","arabic":"عائلة","example":"Our family eats dinner together on Friday.","image_id":"GV-L01-U2-LS1-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U2-LS1-W01"},{"word":"mother","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈmʌðɚ/","definition":"a woman who has a child; mom","arabic":"أم","example":"My mother makes delicious soup.","image_id":"GV-L01-U2-LS1-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U2-LS1-W02"},{"word":"father","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈfɑðɚ/","definition":"a man who has a child; dad","arabic":"أب","example":"His father drives a big truck.","image_id":"GV-L01-U2-LS1-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U2-LS1-W03"},{"word":"brother","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈbrʌðɚ/","definition":"a boy who has the same parents as you","arabic":"أخ","example":"Rakan is my little brother.","image_id":"GV-L01-U2-LS1-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U2-LS1-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"We use my, your, his, her, its, our and their to say who something belongs to. They always come before a noun: my bag, her name.\nUse his for a boy or a man and her for a girl or a woman. The word does not change for plural nouns: my book → my books.\nI → my • you → your • he → his • she → her\nit → its • we → our • they → their\nThe possessive word comes before the noun: my family (NOT family my).","examples":["My uncle is a pilot.","Is this your jacket?","Omar loves his grandpa.","Lina feeds her rabbit every morning.","The bird is in its nest.","Our classroom has a big window.","The twins clean their room on Saturday.","What is your sister's name?"],"common_errors":["✗ This is book my. → ✓ This is my book. (Arabic puts the ending after the noun (كتابي); English puts my before the noun.)","✗ Sara is my sister. His name is Sara. → ✓ Sara is my sister. Her name is Sara. (Use her for a girl.)","✗ The dog wags it's tail. → ✓ The dog wags its tail. (its = belongs to it; it's = it is.)"],"arabic":"نستخدم my وyour وhis وher وits وour وtheir للدلالة على الملكية، وتأتي دائمًا قبل الاسم: my bag.\nفي العربية نضيف الضمير في آخر الكلمة (كتابي)، أما في الإنجليزية فنضع my قبل الاسم: my book.\nhis للمذكر (له)، وher للمؤنث (لها)، وtheir للجمع (لهم).\nلا تخلط بين its (ملكية لغير العاقل) وit's (اختصار it is)."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “This Is My Family: my, your, his, her”. Let’s learn possessive adjectives (my, your, his, her, its, our, their) together.","on_screen":"GV-L01-U2-LS1 | This Is My Family: my, your, his, her","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Listen to the start of “My Family Photo”: Look at my family photo! I am Sara. Look at the green words.","on_screen":"Look at my family photo! I am Sara.","visual":"Image GV-L01-U2-LS1-IMG01 animates gently; target words glow Leaf Green as they are spoken."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"We use my, your, his, her, its, our and their to say who something belongs to. They always come before a noun: my bag, her name. Use his for a boy or a man and her for a girl or a woman. The word does not change for plural nouns: my book → my books.","on_screen":"I → my • you → your • he → his • she → her • it → its • we → our • they → their • The possessive word comes before the noun: my family (NOT family my).","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. My uncle is a pilot. Is this your jacket? Omar loves his grandpa.","on_screen":"My uncle is a pilot. / Is this your jacket? / Omar loves his grandpa.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “This is book my.” That’s not right. We say: “This is my book.”","on_screen":"✗ This is book my.   ✓ This is my book.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: In \"Lina feeds her rabbit\", whose rabbit is it? … Think! … Lina's – so we use *her*. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"my brother\", \"her name\" and \"their house\".","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"my brother\", \"her name\" and \"their house\".","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: possessive adjectives (my, your, his, her, its, our, their).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نستخدم my وyour وhis وher وits وour وtheir للدلالة على الملكية، وتأتي دائمًا قبل الاسم: my bag.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: This is book my. — الصحيح: This is my book.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول my brother وher name وtheir house."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"My Family Photo","body":"Look at my family photo! I am Sara.\nThis is my father. His name is Ahmed. He is tall.\nThis is my mother. Her name is Mona. Her smile is lovely.\nThis is my brother, Ziyad. His bike is red.\nOur baby sister is Dana. Her eyes are big and brown.\nGrandpa Saleh and Grandma Fatimah are in the photo too. Their garden is beautiful.\nI love my family!","word_count":69,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U2-LS1-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS1-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","items":[{"q":"I have a cat. ___ cat is grey.","options":["Her","Your","My","Their"],"answer":"My","explanation":"I → my.","explanation_ar":"الضمير I يصبح my."},{"q":"Ziyad has a new ball. ___ ball is orange.","options":["His","Her","Its","Our"],"answer":"His","explanation":"Use his for a boy or a man.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم his للمذكر."},{"q":"Mona is a nurse. ___ uniform is white.","options":["Her","My","Its","His"],"answer":"Her","explanation":"Use her for a girl or a woman.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم her للمؤنث."},{"q":"We have a garden. ___ garden is small.","options":["Their","His","Your","Our"],"answer":"Our","explanation":"we → our.","explanation_ar":"الضمير we يصبح our."},{"q":"The children have bikes. ___ bikes are fast.","options":["His","Its","Our","Their"],"answer":"Their","explanation":"they → their.","explanation_ar":"الضمير they يصبح their."},{"q":"The rabbit is hungry. ___ food is in the box.","options":["Her","Its","Their","It's"],"answer":"Its","explanation":"Use its for an animal or a thing (no apostrophe).","explanation_ar":"نستخدم its لغير العاقل بدون فاصلة علوية."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS1-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Write the correct word: my, your, his, her, our or their. Word bank: His, Our, Her","items":[{"q":"Adam is from Malaysia. ______ house is near the sea.","options":[],"answer":"His","explanation":"Use his for a boy or a man.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم his للمذكر."},{"q":"Dana is a baby. ______ toys are soft.","options":[],"answer":"Her","explanation":"Use her for a girl or a woman.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم her للمؤنث."},{"q":"We are brothers. ______ dad is a doctor.","options":[],"answer":"Our","explanation":"we → our.","explanation_ar":"الضمير we يصبح our."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS1-B2","type":"order","instructions":"Guided practice: Put the words in order.","items":[{"q":"grandmother / my / is / This   ( . )","options":["grandmother","my","is","This"],"answer":"This is my grandmother.","explanation":"Word order: The possessive word comes before the noun.","explanation_ar":"ترتيب الكلمات: كلمة الملكية تأتي قبل الاسم."},{"q":"Their / white / is / car   ( . )","options":["Their","white","is","car"],"answer":"Their car is white.","explanation":"Word order: The possessive word comes before the noun.","explanation_ar":"ترتيب الكلمات: كلمة الملكية تأتي قبل الاسم."},{"q":"name / What / your / is   ( ? )","options":["name","What","your","is"],"answer":"What is your name?","explanation":"Word order: you → your.","explanation_ar":"ترتيب الكلمات: الضمير you يصبح your."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS1-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Write about the people.","items":[{"q":"I have a brother/sister. ___ name is ___.","options":[],"answer":"His name is Rakan.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses possessive adjectives (my, your, his, her, its, our, their) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"My father is ___. ___ car is ___.","options":[],"answer":"My father is kind. His car is black.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses possessive adjectives (my, your, his, her, its, our, their) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"My best friend is ___. ___ bag is ___.","options":[],"answer":"My best friend is Saad. His bag is blue.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses possessive adjectives (my, your, his, her, its, our, their) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"My grandparents live in ___. ___ house is ___.","options":[],"answer":"My grandparents live in Taif. Their house is big.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses possessive adjectives (my, your, his, her, its, our, their) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"We are in Class ___. ___ teacher is ___.","options":[],"answer":"We are in Class 3A. Our teacher is Mr. Khalid.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses possessive adjectives (my, your, his, her, its, our, their) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS1-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Draw and write.","items":[{"q":"Draw your family. Write 3 sentences with my and his/her.","options":[],"answer":"This is my mother. Her name is Huda. She is kind.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses possessive adjectives (my, your, his, her, its, our, their) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences about your pet or a favorite animal. Use its.","options":[],"answer":"My cat is white. Its eyes are green.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses possessive adjectives (my, your, his, her, its, our, their) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Ask your partner: \"What is your father's name?\" Write the answer.","options":[],"answer":"His father's name is Khalid.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses possessive adjectives (my, your, his, her, its, our, their) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Four Corners Grammar","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["The teacher says a sentence frame with a cue word and four possible answers (A–D).","Students walk to the corner with the correct answer.","One student in each corner explains the choice in one sentence.","Correct corner scores a point; continue with the next cue."],"data":[{"label":"I → my"},{"label":"you → your"},{"label":"he → his"},{"label":"she → her"},{"label":"it → its"},{"label":"we → our"},{"label":"they → their"},{"label":"Sara → Sara's"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"I love ___ mother.","options":["their","your","his","my"],"answer":"my","explanation":"I → my.","explanation_ar":"الضمير I يصبح my."},{"q":"Rakan is my cousin. ___ hair is short.","options":["His","Her","Their","Its"],"answer":"His","explanation":"Use his for a boy or a man.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم his للمذكر."},{"q":"Huda is my aunt. ___ house is big.","options":["Its","Her","Our","His"],"answer":"Her","explanation":"Use her for a girl or a woman.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم her للمؤنث."},{"q":"You and Faisal are brothers. Is this ___ room?","options":["their","its","your","our"],"answer":"your","explanation":"you → your.","explanation_ar":"الضمير you يصبح your."},{"q":"My grandparents are old. ___ garden is green.","options":["Their","Our","His","Its"],"answer":"Their","explanation":"they → their.","explanation_ar":"الضمير they يصبح their."},{"q":"The bird is in ___ cage.","options":["its","their","his","it's"],"answer":"its","explanation":"Use its for an animal or a thing (no apostrophe).","explanation_ar":"نستخدم its لغير العاقل بدون فاصلة علوية."},{"q":"Saad and I are cousins. ___ grandfather is a farmer.","options":["Your","Their","Our","My"],"answer":"Our","explanation":"we → our.","explanation_ar":"الضمير we يصبح our."},{"q":"","options":["This is my uncle his.","My this is uncle.","This is uncle my.","This is my uncle."],"answer":"This is my uncle.","explanation":"The possessive word comes before the noun.","explanation_ar":"كلمة الملكية تأتي قبل الاسم."},{"q":"Noura is my friend. ___","options":["His eyes are brown.","Its eyes are brown.","Her eyes are brown.","Her eyes is brown."],"answer":"Her eyes are brown.","explanation":"Use her for a girl or a woman.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم her للمؤنث."},{"q":"","options":["The cat drinks it's milk.","The cat drinks its milk.","The cat drinks his milk it.","The cat drinks milk its."],"answer":"The cat drinks its milk.","explanation":"Use its for an animal or a thing (no apostrophe).","explanation_ar":"نستخدم its لغير العاقل بدون فاصلة علوية."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS1-IMG01","prompt":"Sara holding a big family photo in her living room: her father, mother, brother Ziyad, baby sister Dana and her grandparents smiling in a garden. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Sara holding a big family photo in her living room: her father, mother, brother Ziyad, baby sister Dana and her grandparents smiling in a garden"},{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS1-IMG02","prompt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about possessive adjectives (my, your, his, her, its, our, their), with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right; leave large empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about possessive adjectives (my, your, his, her, its, our, their), with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right"},{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS1-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows family (a group of people: parents, children, grandparents and more); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing family: a group of people: parents, children, grandparents and more"},{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS1-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows mother (a woman who has a child; mom); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing mother: a woman who has a child; mom"},{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS1-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows father (a man who has a child; dad); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing father: a man who has a child; dad"},{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS1-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows brother (a boy who has the same parents as you); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing brother: a boy who has the same parents as you"},{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS1-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Four Corners Grammar”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Four Corners Grammar"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U2-LS1-W01","script":"family. family. Our family eats dinner together on Friday.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U2-LS1-W02","script":"mother. mother. My mother makes delicious soup.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U2-LS1-W03","script":"father. father. His father drives a big truck.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U2-LS1-W04","script":"brother. brother. Rakan is my little brother.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U2-LS1-T1","script":"Look at my family photo! I am Sara. This is my father. His name is Ahmed. He is tall. This is my mother. Her name is Mona. Her smile is lovely. This is my brother, Ziyad. His bike is red. Our baby sister is Dana. Her eyes are big and brown. Grandpa Saleh and Grandma Fatimah are in the photo too. Their garden is beautiful. I love my family!","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U2-LS1-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “This Is My Family: my, your, his, her”. Let’s learn possessive adjectives (my, your, his, her, its, our, their) together. Listen to the start of “My Family Photo”: Look at my family photo! I am Sara. Look at the green words. We use my, your, his, her, its, our and their to say who something belongs to. They always come before a noun: my bag, her name. Use his for a boy or a man and her for a girl or a woman. The word does not change for plural nouns: my book → my books. Here are some examples. My uncle is a pilot. Is this your jacket? Omar loves his grandpa. Be careful! Some learners say: “This is book my.” That’s not right. We say: “This is my book.” Quick check: In \"Lina feeds her rabbit\", whose rabbit is it? … Think! … Lina's – so we use *her*. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"my brother\", \"her name\" and \"their house\".","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS2","title":"Whose Is It? 's and Who/Whose Questions","objectives":["Students will be able to use 's to show who something belongs to.","Students will be able to ask and answer Who…? and Whose…? questions.","I can say \"Omar's bike\" and \"my sister's room\".","I can ask \"Whose is it?\" and \"Who is he?\"."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام 's للدلالة على الملكية.","سيتمكن الطلاب من طرح أسئلة Who وWhose والإجابة عنها.","أستطيع أن أقول Omar's bike وmy sister's room.","أستطيع أن أسأل Whose is it? وWho is he?"],"vocabulary":[{"word":"sister","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈsɪstɚ/","definition":"a girl who has the same parents as you","arabic":"أخت","example":"Her sister loves painting.","image_id":"GV-L01-U2-LS2-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U2-LS2-W01"},{"word":"grandmother","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɡrændˌmʌðɚ/","definition":"the mother of your mother or father; grandma","arabic":"جدة","example":"Grandmother tells us stories at night.","image_id":"GV-L01-U2-LS2-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U2-LS2-W02"},{"word":"grandfather","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɡrændˌfɑðɚ/","definition":"the father of your mother or father; grandpa","arabic":"جد","example":"My grandfather has a beautiful garden.","image_id":"GV-L01-U2-LS2-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U2-LS2-W03"},{"word":"uncle","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈʌŋkəl/","definition":"the brother of your mother or father","arabic":"عم / خال","example":"Uncle Saad visits us every week.","image_id":"GV-L01-U2-LS2-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U2-LS2-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"To show that something belongs to a person, add 's to the person: Omar's bike = the bike of Omar.\nAsk Whose…? to find the owner of a thing. Ask Who…? to find out about a person.\nAnswer with 's or a possessive word: Whose cap is this? – It's Adam's. / It's his.","examples":["This is Lina's camera.","Dad's shoes are by the door.","My brother's room is messy.","Whose scarf is this? – It's Grandma's.","Who is that man? – He's my uncle.","The baby's bottle is warm.","Whose pencils are these? – They're Noura's.","Who is your English teacher? – Ms. Huda."],"common_errors":["✗ The car of my father is new. → ✓ My father's car is new. (For people, English usually uses 's, not \"the … of …\".)","✗ This is Sara her bag. → ✓ This is Sara's bag. (Don't add her; use 's.)","✗ Who is this bag? → ✓ Whose bag is this? (Ask Whose for the owner.)"],"arabic":"نضيف 's بعد اسم الشخص لنعبّر عن الملكية: Omar's bike = دراجة عمر.\nلا نقول The car of my father، بل نقول My father's car.\nنسأل Whose عن المالك (لمن هذا؟)، ونسأل Who عن الشخص (مَن هذا؟)."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Whose Is It? 's and Who/Whose Questions”. Let’s learn possessive 's, Who…? and Whose…? together.","on_screen":"GV-L01-U2-LS2 | Whose Is It? 's and Who/Whose Questions","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Remember these patterns: This is Sara's book. • My uncle's car is fast. It isn't Omar's cap. It's Yusuf's. Whose cap is this? – It's Adam's. • Who is he? – He's my cousin.","on_screen":"This is Sara's book. • My uncle's car is fast. | It isn't Omar's cap. It's Yusuf's. | Whose cap is this? – It's Adam's. • Who is he? – He's my cousin.","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"To show that something belongs to a person, add 's to the person: Omar's bike = the bike of Omar. Ask Whose…? to find the owner of a thing. Ask Who…? to find out about a person.","on_screen":"possessive 's, Who…? and Whose…?","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. This is Lina's camera. Dad's shoes are by the door. My brother's room is messy.","on_screen":"This is Lina's camera. / Dad's shoes are by the door. / My brother's room is messy.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “The car of my father is new.” That’s not right. We say: “My father's car is new.” For people, English usually uses 's, not \"the … of …\".","on_screen":"✗ The car of my father is new.   ✓ My father's car is new.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"Lina's camera\" – who has the camera? … Think! … Lina. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"Omar's bike\" and \"my sister's room\".","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"Omar's bike\" and \"my sister's room\".","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: possessive 's, Who…? and Whose…?.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نضيف 's بعد اسم الشخص لنعبّر عن الملكية: Omar's bike = دراجة عمر.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: The car of my father is new. — الصحيح: My father's car is new.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول Omar's bike وmy sister's room."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS2-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"This is ___ book. (It belongs to Yusuf.)","options":["Yusuf his","Yusuf's","Yusuf","Yusufs"],"answer":"Yusuf's","explanation":"Add 's to the person to show who has the thing.","explanation_ar":"أضف 's للشخص لتدل على الملكية."},{"q":"___ jacket is this? – It's Rakan's.","options":["Who","Whose","What","Who's"],"answer":"Whose","explanation":"Ask Whose to find the owner.","explanation_ar":"نسأل بـ Whose عن المالك."},{"q":"___ is that girl? – She's my cousin.","options":["Who","Where","Whose","What"],"answer":"Who","explanation":"Ask Who to ask about a person.","explanation_ar":"نسأل بـ Who عن الشخص."},{"q":"My ___ house is near the mosque.","options":["grandpa his","grandpa","grandpa's","grandpas"],"answer":"grandpa's","explanation":"Add 's to the person to show who has the thing.","explanation_ar":"أضف 's للشخص لتدل على الملكية."},{"q":"Whose bottle is this? – It's ___.","options":["Majed","Majeds'","Majed his","Majed's"],"answer":"Majed's","explanation":"Add 's to the person to show who has the thing.","explanation_ar":"أضف 's للشخص لتدل على الملكية."},{"q":"","options":["Mom's phone is on the table.","The phone of Mom is on the table.","Moms phone is on the table.","Mom her phone is on the table."],"answer":"Mom's phone is on the table.","explanation":"Add 's to the person to show who has the thing.","explanation_ar":"أضف 's للشخص لتدل على الملكية."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS2-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Write the answer with 's.","items":[{"q":"the ball / Turki  ('s)","options":[],"answer":"Turki's ball","explanation":"Add 's to the person to show who has the thing.","explanation_ar":"أضف 's للشخص لتدل على الملكية."},{"q":"the garden / my aunt  ('s)","options":[],"answer":"my aunt's garden","explanation":"Add 's to the person to show who has the thing.","explanation_ar":"أضف 's للشخص لتدل على الملكية."},{"q":"the toy / the baby  ('s)","options":[],"answer":"the baby's toy","explanation":"Add 's to the person to show who has the thing.","explanation_ar":"أضف 's للشخص لتدل على الملكية."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS2-B2","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Write Who or Whose. Word bank: Whose, Who","items":[{"q":"______ umbrella is this?","options":[],"answer":"Whose","explanation":"Ask Whose to find the owner.","explanation_ar":"نسأل بـ Whose عن المالك."},{"q":"______ is your best friend?","options":[],"answer":"Who","explanation":"Ask Who to ask about a person.","explanation_ar":"نسأل بـ Who عن الشخص."},{"q":"______ shoes are these?","options":[],"answer":"Whose","explanation":"Ask Whose to find the owner.","explanation_ar":"نسأل بـ Whose عن المالك."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS2-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Answer the questions about you.","items":[{"q":"Who is your favorite teacher?","options":[],"answer":"My favorite teacher is Mr. Khalid.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses possessive 's, Who…? and Whose…? correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Who is the youngest person in your family?","options":[],"answer":"My baby brother is the youngest.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses possessive 's, Who…? and Whose…? correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Whose bag is next to you?","options":[],"answer":"It's Faisal's bag.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses possessive 's, Who…? and Whose…? correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"What is your mother's favorite food?","options":[],"answer":"My mother's favorite food is kabsa.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses possessive 's, Who…? and Whose…? correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Who is your father's brother?","options":[],"answer":"He is my uncle, Uncle Fahad.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses possessive 's, Who…? and Whose…? correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS2-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Play and write.","items":[{"q":"Put 3 things from your desk in a box. Ask \"Whose … is this?\" Write 3 answers.","options":[],"answer":"It's Saad's pen. It's Ali's eraser. It's my ruler.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses possessive 's, Who…? and Whose…? correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 3 sentences about your family with 's.","options":[],"answer":"My sister's name is Reem. My dad's car is grey. My grandma's kitchen is big.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses possessive 's, Who…? and Whose…? correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 Who questions for your partner.","options":[],"answer":"Who is your uncle? Who is your best friend?","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses possessive 's, Who…? and Whose…? correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Grammar Snakes & Ladders","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["Roll and move. If you land on a cue square, make a sentence with the cue and possessive 's, Who…? and Whose…?.","Correct at the bottom of a ladder: climb. Incorrect at the head of a snake: slide down.","Teammates are the judges and must explain any correction.","First player to reach square 30 wins."],"data":[{"cue":"Omar / bike / 's"},{"cue":"Grandma / garden / 's"},{"cue":"Who / your uncle / ?"},{"cue":"Whose / pen / ?"},{"cue":"Dad / car / 's"},{"cue":"the baby / toy / 's"},{"cue":"Whose / bag / ?"},{"cue":"Who / she / ?"},{"cue":"Lina / cat / 's"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"This is my ___ room.","options":["sister","sisters","sister her","sister's"],"answer":"sister's","explanation":"Add 's to the person to show who has the thing.","explanation_ar":"أضف 's للشخص لتدل على الملكية."},{"q":"___ book is this? – It's Noura's.","options":["Who","Where","Whose","Who's"],"answer":"Whose","explanation":"Ask Whose to find the owner.","explanation_ar":"نسأل بـ Whose عن المالك."},{"q":"___ is your grandfather? – He's that man in the garden.","options":["What","Whose","Who","How"],"answer":"Who","explanation":"Ask Who to ask about a person.","explanation_ar":"نسأل بـ Who عن الشخص."},{"q":"Whose cat is it? – It's ___.","options":["Linas","Lina","Lina her","Lina's"],"answer":"Lina's","explanation":"Add 's to the person to show who has the thing.","explanation_ar":"أضف 's للشخص لتدل على الملكية."},{"q":"","options":["Uncle Saad's car is new.","Uncle Saad his car is new.","The car of Uncle Saad is new.","Uncle Saads car is new."],"answer":"Uncle Saad's car is new.","explanation":"Add 's to the person to show who has the thing.","explanation_ar":"أضف 's للشخص لتدل على الملكية."},{"q":"___ that? – It's my cousin, Hamad.","options":["Who","Who's","Whose","What's"],"answer":"Who's","explanation":"Ask Who to ask about a person.","explanation_ar":"نسأل بـ Who عن الشخص."},{"q":"","options":["Who's pencil is this?","Whose pencil is this?","Who pencil is this?","Whose is pencil this?"],"answer":"Whose pencil is this?","explanation":"Ask Whose to find the owner.","explanation_ar":"نسأل بـ Whose عن المالك."},{"q":"Is this Ali's hat? – No, it isn't. It's ___.","options":["Bandars","Bandar his","Bandar","Bandar's"],"answer":"Bandar's","explanation":"Add 's to the person to show who has the thing.","explanation_ar":"أضف 's للشخص لتدل على الملكية."},{"q":"","options":["Dana is the baby's name.","Dana is baby name's.","Dana is the babys name.","Dana is the name of the baby her."],"answer":"Dana is the baby's name.","explanation":"Add 's to the person to show who has the thing.","explanation_ar":"أضف 's للشخص لتدل على الملكية."},{"q":"Whose glasses are these? – ___","options":["They're Grandpa.","It's Grandpa his.","They're Grandpa's.","Who is Grandpa."],"answer":"They're Grandpa's.","explanation":"Add 's to the person to show who has the thing.","explanation_ar":"أضف 's للشخص لتدل على الملكية."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS2-IMG01","prompt":"A lost-and-found box at school with a red cap, a green water bottle and a book; Omar holding up the cap and asking \"Whose is it?\". Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A lost-and-found box at school with a red cap, a green water bottle and a book; Omar holding up the cap and asking \"Whose is it?\""},{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS2-IMG02","prompt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of possessive 's, Who…? and Whose…?: a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “My Family”; empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of possessive 's, Who…? and Whose…?: a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “My Family”"},{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS2-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows sister (a girl who has the same parents as you); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing sister: a girl who has the same parents as you"},{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS2-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows grandmother (the mother of your mother or father; grandma); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing grandmother: the mother of your mother or father; grandma"},{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS2-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows grandfather (the father of your mother or father; grandpa); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing grandfather: the father of your mother or father; grandpa"},{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS2-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows uncle (the brother of your mother or father); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing uncle: the brother of your mother or father"},{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS2-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Grammar Snakes & Ladders”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Grammar Snakes & Ladders"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U2-LS2-W01","script":"sister. sister. Her sister loves painting.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U2-LS2-W02","script":"grandmother. grandmother. Grandmother tells us stories at night.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U2-LS2-W03","script":"grandfather. grandfather. My grandfather has a beautiful garden.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U2-LS2-W04","script":"uncle. uncle. Uncle Saad visits us every week.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U2-LS2-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Whose Is It? 's and Who/Whose Questions”. Let’s learn possessive 's, Who…? and Whose…? together. Remember these patterns: This is Sara's book. • My uncle's car is fast. It isn't Omar's cap. It's Yusuf's. Whose cap is this? – It's Adam's. • Who is he? – He's my cousin. To show that something belongs to a person, add 's to the person: Omar's bike = the bike of Omar. Ask Whose…? to find the owner of a thing. Ask Who…? to find out about a person. Here are some examples. This is Lina's camera. Dad's shoes are by the door. My brother's room is messy. Be careful! Some learners say: “The car of my father is new.” That’s not right. We say: “My father's car is new.” For people, English usually uses 's, not \"the … of …\". Quick check: \"Lina's camera\" – who has the camera? … Think! … Lina. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"Omar's bike\" and \"my sister's room\".","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS3","title":"Family Words: Who Is Who?","objectives":["Students will be able to name family members in English.","Students will be able to sort family words into male and female pairs and explain uncle, aunt and cousin.","I can name the people in my family.","I can explain who my uncle, aunt and cousin are."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من تسمية أفراد العائلة بالإنجليزية.","سيتمكن الطلاب من تصنيف كلمات العائلة إلى أزواج مذكر ومؤنث وشرح uncle وaunt وcousin.","أستطيع أن أسمّي أفراد عائلتي.","أستطيع أن أشرح مَن هو uncle وaunt وcousin."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"aunt","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ænt/","definition":"the sister of your mother or father","arabic":"عمة / خالة","example":"Aunt Maha bakes cookies for us.","image_id":"GV-L01-U2-LS3-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U2-LS3-W01"},{"word":"cousin","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈkʌzən/","definition":"the child of your uncle or aunt","arabic":"ابن/ابنة العم أو الخال","example":"My cousin and I play football.","image_id":"GV-L01-U2-LS3-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U2-LS3-W02"},{"word":"baby","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈbeɪbi/","definition":"a very young child","arabic":"طفل رضيع","example":"The baby is sleeping in her bed.","image_id":"GV-L01-U2-LS3-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U2-LS3-W03"},{"word":"parents","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈpɛrənts/","definition":"your mother and father","arabic":"الوالدان","example":"My parents are kind and funny.","image_id":"GV-L01-U2-LS3-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U2-LS3-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"Family words often come in pairs: one word for males and one for females – brother / sister, father / mother.\nEnglish has ONE word for both sides of the family. Uncle can be عم or خال, and aunt can be عمة or خالة. Cousin is for boys and girls.\nShort, friendly words: mom, dad, grandma, grandpa. Parents = mother + father.\nCollocations/phrases: father ↔ mother • brother ↔ sister • grandfather ↔ grandmother | uncle ↔ aunt • son ↔ daughter • grandson ↔ granddaughter | same word for boys and girls: cousin • baby • parent • child","examples":["My aunt is my mother's sister.","My uncle is my father's brother.","Hamad is my cousin; his father is my uncle.","Grandma and Grandpa live in Abha.","My parents are at work.","The baby is my little sister.","Noura is Grandpa Saleh's granddaughter.","There are six people in my family."],"common_errors":["✗ My uncle's son is my brother. → ✓ My uncle's son is my cousin. (In English, your uncle's child is your cousin.)","✗ She is my uncle. → ✓ She is my aunt. (aunt = female; uncle = male.)","✗ My parents is kind. → ✓ My parents are kind. (parents = two people → are.)"],"arabic":"في الإنجليزية كلمة uncle تعني العم والخال، وكلمة aunt تعني العمة والخالة.\nكلمة cousin تعني ابن أو ابنة العم أو الخال أو العمة أو الخالة.\nparents تعني الوالدين (الأب والأم) وهي جمع، لذلك نستخدم معها are."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Family Words: Who Is Who?”. Let’s learn family words and male/female pairs together.","on_screen":"GV-L01-U2-LS3 | Family Words: Who Is Who?","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Meet some new words. aunt: the sister of your mother or father. cousin: the child of your uncle or aunt. baby: a very young child.","on_screen":"aunt | cousin | baby","visual":"Each word card flips over to show its picture (vocabulary image briefs) and Arabic meaning."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Family words often come in pairs: one word for males and one for females – brother / sister, father / mother. English has ONE word for both sides of the family. Uncle can be عم or خال, and aunt can be عمة or خالة. Cousin is for boys and girls.","on_screen":"family words and male/female pairs","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. My aunt is my mother's sister. My uncle is my father's brother. Hamad is my cousin; his father is my uncle.","on_screen":"My aunt is my mother's sister. / My uncle is my father's brother. / Hamad is my cousin; his father is my uncle.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “My uncle's son is my brother.” That’s not right. We say: “My uncle's son is my cousin.” In English, your uncle's child is your cousin.","on_screen":"✗ My uncle's son is my brother.   ✓ My uncle's son is my cousin.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: Your father's brother – uncle or aunt? … Think! … Uncle. Great job! Now you can say: I can name the people in my family.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can name the people in my family.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: family words and male/female pairs.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","في الإنجليزية كلمة uncle تعني العم والخال، وكلمة aunt تعني العمة والخالة.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: My uncle's son is my brother. — الصحيح: My uncle's son is my cousin.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أسمّي أفراد عائلتي."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS3-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","items":[{"q":"brother ↔ ___","options":["parents","sister","baby","aunt"],"answer":"sister","explanation":"Choose the word with the right gender (male or female).","explanation_ar":"اختر الكلمة المناسبة للمذكر أو المؤنث."},{"q":"grandfather ↔ ___","options":["cousin","mother","aunt","grandmother"],"answer":"grandmother","explanation":"Choose the word with the right gender (male or female).","explanation_ar":"اختر الكلمة المناسبة للمذكر أو المؤنث."},{"q":"uncle ↔ ___","options":["sister","grandma","aunt","cousin"],"answer":"aunt","explanation":"Choose the word with the right gender (male or female).","explanation_ar":"اختر الكلمة المناسبة للمذكر أو المؤنث."},{"q":"My mother's sister is my ___.","options":["aunt","grandma","uncle","cousin"],"answer":"aunt","explanation":"Think about the family tree: who is the parent of whom?","explanation_ar":"فكّر في شجرة العائلة."},{"q":"My aunt's son is my ___.","options":["cousin","nephew","uncle","brother"],"answer":"cousin","explanation":"Your uncle's or aunt's child is your cousin.","explanation_ar":"ابن العم أو الخال يسمّى cousin."},{"q":"My mother and my father are my ___.","options":["uncles","cousins","parents","babies"],"answer":"parents","explanation":"parents = mother + father (plural → are).","explanation_ar":"parents تعني الوالدين وهي جمع."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS3-B1","type":"match","instructions":"Guided practice: Match the word to its meaning.","items":[{"q":"grandfather","options":["my uncle's daughter","my father's father","my father's sister","a very young child","my mother's brother","my mom and dad"],"answer":"my father's father","explanation":"grandfather → my father's father. Choose the word with the right gender (male or female).","explanation_ar":"اختر الكلمة المناسبة للمذكر أو المؤنث."},{"q":"aunt","options":["my uncle's daughter","my father's father","my father's sister","a very young child","my mother's brother","my mom and dad"],"answer":"my father's sister","explanation":"aunt → my father's sister. Choose the word with the right gender (male or female).","explanation_ar":"اختر الكلمة المناسبة للمذكر أو المؤنث."},{"q":"cousin","options":["my uncle's daughter","my father's father","my father's sister","a very young child","my mother's brother","my mom and dad"],"answer":"my uncle's daughter","explanation":"cousin → my uncle's daughter. Choose the word with the right gender (male or female).","explanation_ar":"اختر الكلمة المناسبة للمذكر أو المؤنث."},{"q":"parents","options":["my uncle's daughter","my father's father","my father's sister","a very young child","my mother's brother","my mom and dad"],"answer":"my mom and dad","explanation":"parents → my mom and dad. Choose the word with the right gender (male or female).","explanation_ar":"اختر الكلمة المناسبة للمذكر أو المؤنث."},{"q":"baby","options":["my uncle's daughter","my father's father","my father's sister","a very young child","my mother's brother","my mom and dad"],"answer":"a very young child","explanation":"baby → a very young child. Choose the word with the right gender (male or female).","explanation_ar":"اختر الكلمة المناسبة للمذكر أو المؤنث."},{"q":"uncle","options":["my uncle's daughter","my father's father","my father's sister","a very young child","my mother's brother","my mom and dad"],"answer":"my mother's brother","explanation":"uncle → my mother's brother. Choose the word with the right gender (male or female).","explanation_ar":"اختر الكلمة المناسبة للمذكر أو المؤنث."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS3-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Write about your family.","items":[{"q":"My grandfather's name is ___.","options":[],"answer":"My grandfather's name is Saleh.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses family words and male/female pairs correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"I have ___ cousins.","options":[],"answer":"I have nine cousins.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses family words and male/female pairs correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"My uncle lives in ___.","options":[],"answer":"My uncle lives in Jeddah.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses family words and male/female pairs correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"My aunt likes ___.","options":[],"answer":"My aunt likes reading.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses family words and male/female pairs correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"In my family there are ___ people.","options":[],"answer":"In my family there are six people.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses family words and male/female pairs correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS3-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Make a family tree.","items":[{"q":"Draw your family tree. Write names and family words.","options":[],"answer":"Grandpa Saleh – Dad – Me – Uncle Fahad – my cousin Hamad","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses family words and male/female pairs correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 3 sentences about your tree.","options":[],"answer":"Saleh is my grandfather. Fahad is my uncle. Hamad is my cousin.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses family words and male/female pairs correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Tell your partner about one cousin. Write 2 sentences.","options":[],"answer":"My cousin is Rakan. He is funny.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses family words and male/female pairs correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Word Dominoes","mechanic":"matching","rules":["Deal the dominoes equally in teams of four.","Player 1 places a domino; the next player adds a domino whose word matches the open definition.","If you cannot play, pass.","The first player with no dominoes left wins."],"data":[{"word":"family","match":"a group of people: parents, children, grandparents and more","arabic":"عائلة"},{"word":"mother","match":"a woman who has a child; mom","arabic":"أم"},{"word":"father","match":"a man who has a child; dad","arabic":"أب"},{"word":"brother","match":"a boy who has the same parents as you","arabic":"أخ"},{"word":"sister","match":"a girl who has the same parents as you","arabic":"أخت"},{"word":"grandmother","match":"the mother of your mother or father; grandma","arabic":"جدة"},{"word":"grandfather","match":"the father of your mother or father; grandpa","arabic":"جد"},{"word":"uncle","match":"the brother of your mother or father","arabic":"عم / خال"},{"word":"aunt","match":"the sister of your mother or father","arabic":"عمة / خالة"},{"word":"cousin","match":"the child of your uncle or aunt","arabic":"ابن/ابنة العم أو الخال"},{"word":"baby","match":"a very young child","arabic":"طفل رضيع"},{"word":"parents","match":"your mother and father","arabic":"الوالدان"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"My father's mother is my ___.","options":["grandmother","mother","aunt","sister"],"answer":"grandmother","explanation":"Think about the family tree: who is the parent of whom?","explanation_ar":"فكّر في شجرة العائلة."},{"q":"sister ↔ ___","options":["parents","brother","uncle","cousin"],"answer":"brother","explanation":"Choose the word with the right gender (male or female).","explanation_ar":"اختر الكلمة المناسبة للمذكر أو المؤنث."},{"q":"My uncle's daughter is my ___.","options":["niece","cousin","aunt","sister"],"answer":"cousin","explanation":"Your uncle's or aunt's child is your cousin.","explanation_ar":"ابن العم أو الخال يسمّى cousin."},{"q":"My ___ are at home. (Mom and Dad)","options":["uncles","parent","cousins","parents"],"answer":"parents","explanation":"parents = mother + father (plural → are).","explanation_ar":"parents تعني الوالدين وهي جمع."},{"q":"My mother's brother is my ___.","options":["uncle","aunt","grandpa","cousin"],"answer":"uncle","explanation":"Think about the family tree: who is the parent of whom?","explanation_ar":"فكّر في شجرة العائلة."},{"q":"A very young child is a ___.","options":["grandpa","cousin","baby","parent"],"answer":"baby","explanation":"Think about the family tree: who is the parent of whom?","explanation_ar":"فكّر في شجرة العائلة."},{"q":"She is my ___. Her name is Aunt Maha.","options":["grandpa","brother","aunt","uncle"],"answer":"aunt","explanation":"Choose the word with the right gender (male or female).","explanation_ar":"اختر الكلمة المناسبة للمذكر أو المؤنث."},{"q":"In English, عم and خال are both ___.","options":["uncle","grandpa","aunt","cousin"],"answer":"uncle","explanation":"Think about the family tree: who is the parent of whom?","explanation_ar":"فكّر في شجرة العائلة."},{"q":"My grandpa's son is my father or my ___.","options":["cousin","grandpa","brother","uncle"],"answer":"uncle","explanation":"Think about the family tree: who is the parent of whom?","explanation_ar":"فكّر في شجرة العائلة."},{"q":"","options":["My parents am kind.","My parents is kind.","My parents are kind.","My parent are kind."],"answer":"My parents are kind.","explanation":"parents = mother + father (plural → are).","explanation_ar":"parents تعني الوالدين وهي جمع."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS3-IMG01","prompt":"A simple family tree on a classroom wall with small pictures of grandparents, parents, uncles, aunts, children and cousins, Zaki pointing with his wing. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A simple family tree on a classroom wall with small pictures of grandparents, parents, uncles, aunts, children and cousins, Zaki pointing with his wing"},{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS3-IMG02","prompt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 4 small picture icons of the lesson words; empty labels. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 4 small picture icons of the lesson words"},{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS3-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows aunt (the sister of your mother or father); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing aunt: the sister of your mother or father"},{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS3-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows cousin (the child of your uncle or aunt); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing cousin: the child of your uncle or aunt"},{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS3-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows baby (a very young child); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing baby: a very young child"},{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS3-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows parents (your mother and father); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing parents: your mother and father"},{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS3-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Word Dominoes”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Word Dominoes"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U2-LS3-W01","script":"aunt. aunt. Aunt Maha bakes cookies for us.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U2-LS3-W02","script":"cousin. cousin. My cousin and I play football.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U2-LS3-W03","script":"baby. baby. The baby is sleeping in her bed.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U2-LS3-W04","script":"parents. parents. My parents are kind and funny.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U2-LS3-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Family Words: Who Is Who?”. Let’s learn family words and male/female pairs together. Meet some new words. aunt: the sister of your mother or father. cousin: the child of your uncle or aunt. baby: a very young child. Family words often come in pairs: one word for males and one for females – brother / sister, father / mother. English has ONE word for both sides of the family. Uncle can be عم or خال, and aunt can be عمة or خالة. Cousin is for boys and girls. Here are some examples. My aunt is my mother's sister. My uncle is my father's brother. Hamad is my cousin; his father is my uncle. Be careful! Some learners say: “My uncle's son is my brother.” That’s not right. We say: “My uncle's son is my cousin.” In English, your uncle's child is your cousin. Quick check: Your father's brother – uncle or aunt? … Think! … Uncle. Great job! Now you can say: I can name the people in my family.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS4","title":"Capital Letters for Names","objectives":["Students will be able to write people's and pets' names with capital letters.","Students will be able to write titles (Mr., Mrs., Ms., Dr.) correctly before names.","I can write names with capital letters.","I can write Mr., Mrs., Ms. and Dr. before a name."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة أسماء الأشخاص والحيوانات الأليفة بحرف كبير.","سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة الألقاب Mr. وMrs. وMs. وDr. بشكل صحيح.","أستطيع أن أكتب الأسماء بحرف كبير.","أستطيع أن أكتب Mr. وMrs. وMs. وDr. قبل الاسم."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"family","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈfæməli/","definition":"a group of people: parents, children, grandparents and more","arabic":"عائلة","example":"Our family eats dinner together on Friday.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"mother","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈmʌðɚ/","definition":"a woman who has a child; mom","arabic":"أم","example":"My mother makes delicious soup.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"father","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈfɑðɚ/","definition":"a man who has a child; dad","arabic":"أب","example":"His father drives a big truck.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"brother","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈbrʌðɚ/","definition":"a boy who has the same parents as you","arabic":"أخ","example":"Rakan is my little brother.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"sister","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈsɪstɚ/","definition":"a girl who has the same parents as you","arabic":"أخت","example":"Her sister loves painting.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"grandmother","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɡrændˌmʌðɚ/","definition":"the mother of your mother or father; grandma","arabic":"جدة","example":"Grandmother tells us stories at night.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"A name is special, so it starts with a capital letter: Ziyad, Dana, Grandpa Saleh. A pet's name is a name too: our cat Snowy.\nTitles before a name also start with a capital letter and have a period: Mr. (a man), Mrs. (a married woman), Ms. (a woman), Dr. (a doctor).\nFamily words are small letters in the middle of a sentence: my mom, her uncle. When we use them as a name, they start with a capital: Thank you, Mom!\nPeople's names start with a capital letter: Hamad, Reem.\nPets' names start with a capital letter: our parrot Kiwi.\nTitles: Mr., Mrs., Ms., Dr. – capital letter + period.\nFamily words with my/your/his/her are small: my aunt. Used as a name: Aunt Maha, Grandma.","examples":["My cousin's name is Rakan.","Dr. Ahmed is my father.","Our cat's name is Snowy.","Mrs. Mona is our neighbor.","Good morning, Mr. Khalid!","Aunt Maha lives in Riyadh.","My mom is a nurse.","Thank you, Dad!"],"common_errors":["✗ my brother is ziyad. → ✓ My brother is Ziyad. (Capital letters for the first word and for names.)","✗ mr khalid is our teacher. → ✓ Mr. Khalid is our teacher. (Mr. has a capital M and a period.)","✗ My Mom is a nurse. → ✓ My mom is a nurse. (After my, mom is not a name, so it is small.)"],"arabic":"أسماء الأشخاص والحيوانات الأليفة تبدأ دائمًا بحرف كبير: Ziyad، Snowy.\nالألقاب Mr. وMrs. وMs. وDr. تبدأ بحرف كبير وتنتهي بنقطة.\nكلمة mom بعد my تُكتب صغيرة، لكن عندما نناديها كاسم نكتبها كبيرة: Thank you, Mom!"},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Capital Letters for Names”. Let’s learn capital letters for names of people, pets and titles (Mr., Mrs., Ms., Dr.) together.","on_screen":"GV-L01-U2-LS4 | Capital Letters for Names","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"A name is special, so it starts with a capital letter: Ziyad, Dana, Grandpa Saleh. A pet's name is a name too: our cat Snowy.","on_screen":"capital letters for names of people, pets and titles (Mr., Mrs., Ms., Dr.)","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"A name is special, so it starts with a capital letter: Ziyad, Dana, Grandpa Saleh. A pet's name is a name too: our cat Snowy. Titles before a name also start with a capital letter and have a period: Mr. (a man), Mrs. (a married woman), Ms. (a woman), Dr. (a doctor).","on_screen":"People's names start with a capital letter: Hamad, Reem. • Pets' names start with a capital letter: our parrot Kiwi. • Titles: Mr., Mrs., Ms., Dr. – capital letter + period.","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. My cousin's name is Rakan. Dr. Ahmed is my father. Our cat's name is Snowy.","on_screen":"My cousin's name is Rakan. / Dr. Ahmed is my father. / Our cat's name is Snowy.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “my brother is ziyad.” That’s not right. We say: “My brother is Ziyad.” Capital letters for the first word and for names.","on_screen":"✗ my brother is ziyad.   ✓ My brother is Ziyad.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: Do we write \"Mr\" with a period in American English? … Think! … Yes – Mr. with a period. Great job! Now you can say: I can write names with capital letters.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can write names with capital letters.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: capital letters for names of people, pets and titles (Mr., Mrs., Ms., Dr.).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","أسماء الأشخاص والحيوانات الأليفة تبدأ دائمًا بحرف كبير: Ziyad، Snowy.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: my brother is ziyad. — الصحيح: My brother is Ziyad.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أكتب الأسماء بحرف كبير."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"My Family (editing passage)","body":"My name is noura. My father is dr. Fahad. My mother is a teacher. I have a brother. His name is turki. Our cat is snowy I love my family.","word_count":30,"audio_id":""}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS4-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct sentence.","items":[{"q":"","options":["my sister is Reem","My sister is Reem.","My Sister is reem.","my sister is reem."],"answer":"My sister is Reem.","explanation":"Names of people start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"أسماء الأشخاص تبدأ بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["Our dog's name is Max.","our dog's name is Max","Our Dog's name is max.","Our dog's name is max."],"answer":"Our dog's name is Max.","explanation":"A pet's name is a name: capital letter.","explanation_ar":"اسم الحيوان الأليف يبدأ بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["dr. Huda is kind.","dr huda is kind.","Dr huda is kind.","Dr. Huda is kind."],"answer":"Dr. Huda is kind.","explanation":"Titles: Mr., Mrs., Ms., Dr. – capital letter and period.","explanation_ar":"الألقاب بحرف كبير ونقطة."},{"q":"","options":["My aunt is a teacher.","My aunt Is a teacher.","My Aunt is a teacher.","my aunt is a Teacher."],"answer":"My aunt is a teacher.","explanation":"After my/his/her, family words are small letters.","explanation_ar":"كلمات العائلة بعد my تُكتب صغيرة."},{"q":"","options":["hello, mrs. Mona!","Hello, mrs. mona!","Hello, Mrs. Mona!","Hello, Mrs mona!"],"answer":"Hello, Mrs. Mona!","explanation":"Titles: Mr., Mrs., Ms., Dr. – capital letter and period.","explanation_ar":"الألقاب بحرف كبير ونقطة."},{"q":"","options":["Grandma fatimah is funny.","grandma Fatimah is funny","Grandma Fatimah is funny.","grandma fatimah is funny."],"answer":"Grandma Fatimah is funny.","explanation":"Names of people start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"أسماء الأشخاص تبدأ بحرف كبير."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS4-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Correct the mistake.","items":[{"q":"My cousin is hamad.","options":[],"answer":"My cousin is Hamad.","explanation":"hamad → Hamad. Names of people start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: hamad → Hamad. أسماء الأشخاص تبدأ بحرف كبير."},{"q":"Our parrot is called kiwi.","options":[],"answer":"Our parrot is called Kiwi.","explanation":"kiwi → Kiwi. A pet's name is a name: capital letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: kiwi → Kiwi. اسم الحيوان الأليف يبدأ بحرف كبير."},{"q":"mr. Saad is my uncle.","options":[],"answer":"Mr. Saad is my uncle.","explanation":"mr. → Mr.. Titles: Mr., Mrs., Ms., Dr. – capital letter and period.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: mr. → Mr.. الألقاب بحرف كبير ونقطة."},{"q":"My Grandpa is seventy.","options":[],"answer":"My grandpa is seventy.","explanation":"Grandpa → grandpa. After my/his/her, family words are small letters.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: Grandpa → grandpa. كلمات العائلة بعد my تُكتب صغيرة."},{"q":"ms Huda is in the library.","options":[],"answer":"Ms. Huda is in the library.","explanation":"ms → Ms.. Titles: Mr., Mrs., Ms., Dr. – capital letter and period.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: ms → Ms.. الألقاب بحرف كبير ونقطة."},{"q":"her name is Dana.","options":[],"answer":"Her name is Dana.","explanation":"her → Her. Start the sentence with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: her → Her. ابدأ الجملة بحرف كبير."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS4-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Edit the paragraph.","items":[{"q":"My name is noura.","options":[],"answer":"My name is Noura.","explanation":"noura → Noura. Names of people start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: noura → Noura. أسماء الأشخاص تبدأ بحرف كبير."},{"q":"My father is dr. Fahad.","options":[],"answer":"My father is Dr. Fahad.","explanation":"dr. → Dr.. Names of people start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: dr. → Dr.. أسماء الأشخاص تبدأ بحرف كبير."},{"q":"His name is turki.","options":[],"answer":"His name is Turki.","explanation":"turki → Turki. Names of people start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: turki → Turki. أسماء الأشخاص تبدأ بحرف كبير."},{"q":"Our cat is snowy. I love my family.","options":[],"answer":"Our cat is Snowy. I love my family.","explanation":"snowy → Snowy. Names of people start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: snowy → Snowy. أسماء الأشخاص تبدأ بحرف كبير."},{"q":"Our cat is Snowy I love my family.","options":[],"answer":"Our cat is Snowy. I love my family.","explanation":"(add) → .. Names of people start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → .. أسماء الأشخاص تبدأ بحرف كبير."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS4-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write it correctly.","items":[{"q":"Write the names of 3 people in your family with a family word.","options":[],"answer":"Uncle Saad, Aunt Maha, Grandpa Saleh","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses capital letters for names of people, pets and titles (Mr., Mrs., Ms., Dr.) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write the name of a pet (real or pretend) in a sentence.","options":[],"answer":"My cat's name is Lulu.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses capital letters for names of people, pets and titles (Mr., Mrs., Ms., Dr.) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences about teachers or doctors you know. Use Mr., Ms. or Dr.","options":[],"answer":"Mr. Khalid is my teacher. Dr. Reem is kind.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses capital letters for names of people, pets and titles (Mr., Mrs., Ms., Dr.) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Speed Spell","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["The teacher says a word and a short sentence with it.","Students write the word in 10 seconds.","Show boards on \"Show me!\". Correct = 1 point.","After 10 words, partners check each other's boards and correct any mistakes."],"data":[{"word":"mother","clue":"a woman who has a child; mom"},{"word":"father","clue":"a man who has a child; dad"},{"word":"brother","clue":"a boy who has the same parents as you"},{"word":"sister","clue":"a girl who has the same parents as you"},{"word":"uncle","clue":"the brother of your mother or father"},{"word":"cousin","clue":"the child of your uncle or aunt"},{"word":"family","clue":"a group of people: parents, children, grandparents and more"},{"word":"grandmother","clue":"the mother of your mother or father; grandma"},{"word":"grandfather","clue":"the father of your mother or father; grandpa"},{"word":"aunt","clue":"the sister of your mother or father"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"","options":["My uncle is saad.","my uncle is saad.","My uncle is Saad.","My Uncle is saad."],"answer":"My uncle is Saad.","explanation":"Names of people start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"أسماء الأشخاص تبدأ بحرف كبير."},{"q":"Which word needs a capital letter? \"our rabbit is called fluffy.\"","options":["our, fluffy","is, our","rabbit, called","called, fluffy"],"answer":"our, fluffy","explanation":"A pet's name is a name: capital letter.","explanation_ar":"اسم الحيوان الأليف يبدأ بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["mr. Hamad is a pilot.","Mr hamad is a pilot.","Mr. Hamad is a pilot.","mr. hamad is a pilot."],"answer":"Mr. Hamad is a pilot.","explanation":"Titles: Mr., Mrs., Ms., Dr. – capital letter and period.","explanation_ar":"الألقاب بحرف كبير ونقطة."},{"q":"","options":["thank you, Mom!","Thank you, Mom!","thank you, mom!","Thank you, mom"],"answer":"Thank you, Mom!","explanation":"After my/his/her, family words are small letters.","explanation_ar":"كلمات العائلة بعد my تُكتب صغيرة."},{"q":"","options":["His mother is a Doctor.","his mother is a Doctor.","His Mother is a doctor.","His mother is a doctor."],"answer":"His mother is a doctor.","explanation":"After my/his/her, family words are small letters.","explanation_ar":"كلمات العائلة بعد my تُكتب صغيرة."},{"q":"Which title is for a doctor?","options":["Dr.","Ms.","Mr.","Mrs."],"answer":"Dr.","explanation":"Titles: Mr., Mrs., Ms., Dr. – capital letter and period.","explanation_ar":"الألقاب بحرف كبير ونقطة."},{"q":"","options":["Aunt Reem is here.","aunt Reem is here","Aunt reem is here.","aunt reem is here."],"answer":"Aunt Reem is here.","explanation":"Names of people start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"أسماء الأشخاص تبدأ بحرف كبير."},{"q":"How many capital letters are missing? \"my cat is lulu.\"","options":["1","0","3","2"],"answer":"2","explanation":"A pet's name is a name: capital letter.","explanation_ar":"اسم الحيوان الأليف يبدأ بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["Good morning, Ms lama!","good morning, Ms. Lama!","Good morning, ms. lama!","Good morning, Ms. Lama!"],"answer":"Good morning, Ms. Lama!","explanation":"Titles: Mr., Mrs., Ms., Dr. – capital letter and period.","explanation_ar":"الألقاب بحرف كبير ونقطة."},{"q":"","options":["My brother's Name is Bandar.","My brother's name is Bandar.","my brother's name is bandar.","My Brother's name is bandar."],"answer":"My brother's name is Bandar.","explanation":"Names of people start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"أسماء الأشخاص تبدأ بحرف كبير."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS4-IMG01","prompt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “My Family” that shows capital letters for names of people, pets and titles (Mr., Mrs., Ms., Dr.) in action. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “My Family” that shows capital letters for names of people, pets and titles (Mr., Mrs., Ms., Dr.) in action"},{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS4-IMG02","prompt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen"},{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS4-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Speed Spell”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Speed Spell"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U2-LS4-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Capital Letters for Names”. Let’s learn capital letters for names of people, pets and titles (Mr., Mrs., Ms., Dr.) together. A name is special, so it starts with a capital letter: Ziyad, Dana, Grandpa Saleh. A pet's name is a name too: our cat Snowy. A name is special, so it starts with a capital letter: Ziyad, Dana, Grandpa Saleh. A pet's name is a name too: our cat Snowy. Titles before a name also start with a capital letter and have a period: Mr. (a man), Mrs. (a married woman), Ms. (a woman), Dr. (a doctor). Here are some examples. My cousin's name is Rakan. Dr. Ahmed is my father. Our cat's name is Snowy. Be careful! Some learners say: “my brother is ziyad.” That’s not right. We say: “My brother is Ziyad.” Capital letters for the first word and for names. Quick check: Do we write \"Mr\" with a period in American English? … Think! … Yes – Mr. with a period. Great job! Now you can say: I can write names with capital letters.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS5","title":"Our Family Poster: Language in Use","objectives":["Students will be able to present their family using possessives and family words.","Students will be able to write a short family poster with capital letters for names.","I can present my family to my class.","I can write a family poster with my, his, her and 's."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من تقديم عائلاتهم باستخدام أدوات الملكية وكلمات العائلة.","سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة ملصق قصير عن العائلة مع الحروف الكبيرة للأسماء.","أستطيع أن أقدّم عائلتي لزملائي.","أستطيع أن أكتب ملصقًا عن عائلتي باستخدام my وhis وher و's."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"family","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈfæməli/","definition":"a group of people: parents, children, grandparents and more","arabic":"عائلة","example":"Our family eats dinner together on Friday.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"mother","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈmʌðɚ/","definition":"a woman who has a child; mom","arabic":"أم","example":"My mother makes delicious soup.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"father","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈfɑðɚ/","definition":"a man who has a child; dad","arabic":"أب","example":"His father drives a big truck.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"brother","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈbrʌðɚ/","definition":"a boy who has the same parents as you","arabic":"أخ","example":"Rakan is my little brother.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"sister","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈsɪstɚ/","definition":"a girl who has the same parents as you","arabic":"أخت","example":"Her sister loves painting.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"grandmother","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɡrændˌmʌðɚ/","definition":"the mother of your mother or father; grandma","arabic":"جدة","example":"Grandmother tells us stories at night.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"grandfather","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɡrændˌfɑðɚ/","definition":"the father of your mother or father; grandpa","arabic":"جد","example":"My grandfather has a beautiful garden.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"uncle","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈʌŋkəl/","definition":"the brother of your mother or father","arabic":"عم / خال","example":"Uncle Saad visits us every week.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"aunt","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ænt/","definition":"the sister of your mother or father","arabic":"عمة / خالة","example":"Aunt Maha bakes cookies for us.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"cousin","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈkʌzən/","definition":"the child of your uncle or aunt","arabic":"ابن/ابنة العم أو الخال","example":"My cousin and I play football.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"baby","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈbeɪbi/","definition":"a very young child","arabic":"طفل رضيع","example":"The baby is sleeping in her bed.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"parents","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈpɛrənts/","definition":"your mother and father","arabic":"الوالدان","example":"My parents are kind and funny.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Today you use all the language of Unit 2: my, your, his, her, its, our, their, 's, family words and capital letters for names.\nA family poster says who is in the family, gives their names and tells one fun fact about each person.\n✔ This is my… / His name is… / Her name is…\n✔ 's for the owner: my sister's cat\n✔ capital letters for names and titles","examples":["This is my grandpa. His name is Saleh.","My aunt's house is in Madinah.","Our cousins are funny.","My little brother's name is Rakan.","Their car is big and white.","Who is the girl in the photo? – She's my cousin.","Whose bike is it? – It's my dad's.","Her cat is called Tiger."],"common_errors":["✗ This is my father his name is Ahmed. → ✓ This is my father. His name is Ahmed. (Two ideas = two sentences.)","✗ My sister name is Mariam. → ✓ My sister's name is Mariam. (Add 's to the owner.)","✗ My grandparents is in Cairo. → ✓ My grandparents are in Cairo. (grandparents = plural → are.)"],"arabic":"في هذا الدرس نجمع أدوات الملكية my وhis وher و's مع كلمات العائلة والحروف الكبيرة.\nلا تنسَ 's: My sister's name (اسم أختي).\nكل فكرة في جملة مستقلة تبدأ بحرف كبير وتنتهي بنقطة."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Our Family Poster: Language in Use”. Let’s learn possessives ('s and my/his/her), family words and capital letters (unit review) together.","on_screen":"GV-L01-U2-LS5 | Our Family Poster: Language in Use","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Family show-and-tell: show a drawing or photo of your family. Say \"This is my…\", \"His/Her name is…\". Your partner asks \"Who is…?\" and \"Whose … is this?\".","on_screen":"Language in use","visual":"Split screen: two cast members talking, with speech bubbles appearing."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Today you use all the language of Unit 2: my, your, his, her, its, our, their, 's, family words and capital letters for names. A family poster says who is in the family, gives their names and tells one fun fact about each person.","on_screen":"✔ This is my… / His name is… / Her name is… • ✔ 's for the owner: my sister's cat • ✔ capital letters for names and titles","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. This is my grandpa. His name is Saleh. My aunt's house is in Madinah. Our cousins are funny.","on_screen":"This is my grandpa. His name is Saleh. / My aunt's house is in Madinah. / Our cousins are funny.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “This is my father his name is Ahmed.” That’s not right. We say: “This is my father. His name is Ahmed.” Two ideas = two sentences.","on_screen":"✗ This is my father his name is Ahmed.   ✓ This is my father. His name is Ahmed.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: what is wrong with “My sister name is Mariam.”? … Think! … It should be “My sister's name is Mariam.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can present my family to my class.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can present my family to my class.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: possessives ('s and my/his/her), family words and capital letters (unit review).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","في هذا الدرس نجمع أدوات الملكية my وhis وher و's مع كلمات العائلة والحروف الكبيرة.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: This is my father his name is Ahmed. — الصحيح: This is my father. His name is Ahmed.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقدّم عائلتي لزملائي."]},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"My Family – Yusuf","body":"This is my family. My father's name is Mahmoud. He is an engineer.\nMy mother's name is Salma. Her food is delicious!\nI have one sister. Her name is Mariam. Her cat is called Tiger.\nMy grandparents live in Cairo. Their house is old and big.\nI love my family very much.","word_count":52,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L01-U2-LS5-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS5-A1","type":"true_false","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read Yusuf's poster. True or False?","items":[{"q":"Yusuf's father is an engineer.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “My Family – Yusuf”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Yusuf has two sisters.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “My Family – Yusuf”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Mariam's cat is called Tiger.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “My Family – Yusuf”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"His grandparents live in Riyadh.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “My Family – Yusuf”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"His grandparents' house is new and small.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “My Family – Yusuf”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Yusuf's mother is a great cook.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “My Family – Yusuf”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS5-B1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Guided practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"Mariam is Yusuf's sister. ___ cat is called Tiger.","options":["Her","His","Their","Its"],"answer":"Her","explanation":"Use the possessive word for the owner (my, his, her, our, their).","explanation_ar":"استخدم أداة الملكية المناسبة."},{"q":"This is ___ hat. It belongs to my uncle.","options":["my uncle","uncle my","my uncle's","my uncles"],"answer":"my uncle's","explanation":"Add 's to the owner.","explanation_ar":"أضف 's للمالك."},{"q":"My father's father is my ___.","options":["brother","cousin","uncle","grandfather"],"answer":"grandfather","explanation":"Choose the correct family word.","explanation_ar":"اختر كلمة العائلة الصحيحة."},{"q":"","options":["Mr. Mahmoud is an engineer.","mr. Mahmoud is an engineer","mr. mahmoud is an engineer.","Mr mahmoud is an engineer."],"answer":"Mr. Mahmoud is an engineer.","explanation":"Names and titles start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"الأسماء والألقاب تبدأ بحرف كبير."},{"q":"My cousins ___ at our house today.","options":["be","are","am","is"],"answer":"are","explanation":"Use am, is or are to match the subject.","explanation_ar":"استخدم am أو is أو are حسب الفاعل."},{"q":"___ is your aunt? – She's the lady in the blue dress.","options":["Who's","Whose","What","Who"],"answer":"Who","explanation":"Use the possessive word for the owner (my, his, her, our, their).","explanation_ar":"استخدم أداة الملكية المناسبة."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS5-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Talk, then write.","items":[{"q":"Ask your partner: \"Who is in your family?\" Write 2 names.","options":[],"answer":"His brother Fahad and his sister Reem.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses possessives ('s and my/his/her), family words and capital letters (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Ask: \"What is your mother's job?\" Write the answer.","options":[],"answer":"His mother is a teacher.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses possessives ('s and my/his/her), family words and capital letters (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Ask: \"Whose phone is this?\" about a picture. Write the answer.","options":[],"answer":"It's his dad's phone.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses possessives ('s and my/his/her), family words and capital letters (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Ask: \"Who is your favorite cousin?\" Write the answer.","options":[],"answer":"His favorite cousin is Ziyad.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses possessives ('s and my/his/her), family words and capital letters (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Tell your partner one fun fact about your grandparents. Write it.","options":[],"answer":"My grandpa's garden has lemon trees.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses possessives ('s and my/his/her), family words and capital letters (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS5-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write your family poster.","items":[{"q":"Plan: list the people in your family and one fact about each.","options":[],"answer":"Dad – doctor; Mom – kind; sister Reem – loves cats","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses possessives ('s and my/his/her), family words and capital letters (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write your poster in 4–6 sentences.","options":[],"answer":"This is my family. My father's name is Fahad. He is a doctor. My mother's name is Huda. Her smile is lovely. My sister Reem loves cats.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses possessives ('s and my/his/her), family words and capital letters (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Check: capital letters for names? 's? his/her? Fix one mistake.","options":[],"answer":"I changed “my sister name” to “my sister's name”.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses possessives ('s and my/his/her), family words and capital letters (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Spin the Review Wheel","mechanic":"spin_wheel","rules":["A player spins the wheel and lands on a word.","Say what the word means and use it in a sentence with possessives ('s and my/his/her), family words and capital letters (unit review).","Teammates check: meaning (1 point), grammar (1 point), pronunciation (1 point).","Highest total after 6 minutes wins."],"data":[{"cue":"family","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"mother","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"father","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"brother","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"sister","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"grandmother","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"grandfather","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"uncle","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"aunt","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"cousin","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"baby","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"parents","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"This is Omar. ___ dad is a pilot.","options":["Our","His","Its","Her"],"answer":"His","explanation":"Use the possessive word for the owner (my, his, her, our, their).","explanation_ar":"استخدم أداة الملكية المناسبة."},{"q":"","options":["My cousin her name is Lama.","My cousin's name is Lama.","My cousin name is Lama.","My cousins name is lama."],"answer":"My cousin's name is Lama.","explanation":"Add 's to the owner.","explanation_ar":"أضف 's للمالك."},{"q":"My father's sister is my ___.","options":["cousin","uncle","grandma","aunt"],"answer":"aunt","explanation":"Choose the correct family word.","explanation_ar":"اختر كلمة العائلة الصحيحة."},{"q":"","options":["Dr rakan is my uncle.","dr. rakan is my uncle.","dr. Rakan is my uncle","Dr. Rakan is my uncle."],"answer":"Dr. Rakan is my uncle.","explanation":"Names and titles start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"الأسماء والألقاب تبدأ بحرف كبير."},{"q":"The children love ___ grandparents.","options":["his","its","their","our"],"answer":"their","explanation":"Use the possessive word for the owner (my, his, her, our, their).","explanation_ar":"استخدم أداة الملكية المناسبة."},{"q":"___ glasses are these? – They're Grandpa's.","options":["Whose","Who","Who's","What"],"answer":"Whose","explanation":"Add 's to the owner.","explanation_ar":"أضف 's للمالك."},{"q":"My parents ___ happy today.","options":["be","are","am","is"],"answer":"are","explanation":"Use am, is or are to match the subject.","explanation_ar":"استخدم am أو is أو are حسب الفاعل."},{"q":"We live in Taif. ___ house is near a park.","options":["Our","My","Its","Their"],"answer":"Our","explanation":"Use the possessive word for the owner (my, his, her, our, their).","explanation_ar":"استخدم أداة الملكية المناسبة."},{"q":"","options":["The dog is in bed its.","The dog is in it's bed.","The dog is in its bed.","The dog is in his bed it."],"answer":"The dog is in its bed.","explanation":"Use the possessive word for the owner (my, his, her, our, their).","explanation_ar":"استخدم أداة الملكية المناسبة."},{"q":"","options":["My aunt's cat is white.","My aunts cat is white.","My aunt her cat is white.","The cat of my aunt is white her."],"answer":"My aunt's cat is white.","explanation":"Add 's to the owner.","explanation_ar":"أضف 's للمالك."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS5-IMG01","prompt":"Yusuf presenting a hand-drawn family poster to his class, pointing to his grandparents, while classmates listen. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Yusuf presenting a hand-drawn family poster to his class, pointing to his grandparents, while classmates listen"},{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS5-IMG02","prompt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “My Family”, speech bubbles left empty. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “My Family”, speech bubbles left empty"},{"id":"GV-L01-U2-LS5-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Spin the Review Wheel”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Spin the Review Wheel"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U2-LS5-T1","script":"This is my family. My father's name is Mahmoud. He is an engineer. My mother's name is Salma. Her food is delicious! I have one sister. Her name is Mariam. Her cat is called Tiger. My grandparents live in Cairo. Their house is old and big. I love my family very much.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.85"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L01-U2-LS5-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Our Family Poster: Language in Use”. Let’s learn possessives ('s and my/his/her), family words and capital letters (unit review) together. Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Family show-and-tell: show a drawing or photo of your family. Say \"This is my…\", \"His/Her name is…\". Your partner asks \"Who is…?\" and \"Whose … is this?\". Today you use all the language of Unit 2: my, your, his, her, its, our, their, 's, family words and capital letters for names. A family poster says who is in the family, gives their names and tells one fun fact about each person. Here are some examples. This is my grandpa. His name is Saleh. My aunt's house is in Madinah. Our cousins are funny. Be careful! Some learners say: “This is my father his name is Ahmed.” That’s not right. We say: “This is my father. His name is Ahmed.” Two ideas = two sentences. Quick check: what is wrong with “My sister name is Mariam.”? … Think! … It should be “My sister's name is Mariam.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can present my family to my class.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.85"}]}],"unit_test":[{"q":"I have a bike. ___ bike is green.","options":["My","Your","Their","His"],"answer":"My","explanation":"I → my.","explanation_ar":"الضمير I يصبح my."},{"q":"Reem is my sister. ___ room is pink.","options":["Her","His","Our","Its"],"answer":"Her","explanation":"Use her for a girl or a woman.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم her للمؤنث."},{"q":"Bandar is my brother. ___ shoes are new.","options":["Her","Their","His","Its"],"answer":"His","explanation":"Use his for a boy or a man.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم his للمذكر."},{"q":"We love ___ teacher.","options":["your","our","its","their"],"answer":"our","explanation":"we → our.","explanation_ar":"الضمير we يصبح our."},{"q":"The parrot is in ___ cage.","options":["their","her","it's","its"],"answer":"its","explanation":"Use its for an animal or a thing (no apostrophe).","explanation_ar":"نستخدم its لغير العاقل بدون فاصلة علوية."},{"q":"","options":["My this is grandfather.","This is my grandfather.","This is grandfather my.","This my grandfather is."],"answer":"This is my grandfather.","explanation":"The possessive word comes before the noun.","explanation_ar":"كلمة الملكية تأتي قبل الاسم."},{"q":"This is ___ desk. (It belongs to Saad.)","options":["Saad his","Saads","Saad's","Saad"],"answer":"Saad's","explanation":"Add 's to the person to show who has the thing.","explanation_ar":"أضف 's للشخص لتدل على الملكية."},{"q":"___ socks are these? – They're Rakan's.","options":["Who","What","Who's","Whose"],"answer":"Whose","explanation":"Ask Whose to find the owner.","explanation_ar":"نسأل بـ Whose عن المالك."},{"q":"___ is your doctor? – Dr. Huda.","options":["Whose","Who","Which","Where"],"answer":"Who","explanation":"Ask Who to ask about a person.","explanation_ar":"نسأل بـ Who عن الشخص."},{"q":"","options":["The car of my uncle is fast.","My uncle his car is fast.","My uncle's car is fast.","My uncles car is fast."],"answer":"My uncle's car is fast.","explanation":"Add 's to the person to show who has the thing.","explanation_ar":"أضف 's للشخص لتدل على الملكية."},{"q":"My mother's mother is my ___.","options":["aunt","sister","cousin","grandmother"],"answer":"grandmother","explanation":"Think about the family tree: who is the parent of whom?","explanation_ar":"فكّر في شجرة العائلة."},{"q":"Hamad is my uncle's son. He is my ___.","options":["cousin","grandpa","brother","uncle"],"answer":"cousin","explanation":"Your uncle's or aunt's child is your cousin.","explanation_ar":"ابن العم أو الخال يسمّى cousin."},{"q":"son ↔ ___","options":["father","brother","daughter","uncle"],"answer":"daughter","explanation":"Choose the word with the right gender (male or female).","explanation_ar":"اختر الكلمة المناسبة للمذكر أو المؤنث."},{"q":"Mom and Dad are my ___.","options":["uncles","babies","parents","cousins"],"answer":"parents","explanation":"parents = mother + father (plural → are).","explanation_ar":"parents تعني الوالدين وهي جمع."},{"q":"Dana is one year old. She is a ___.","options":["baby","aunt","parent","grandma"],"answer":"baby","explanation":"Think about the family tree: who is the parent of whom?","explanation_ar":"فكّر في شجرة العائلة."},{"q":"In English, عمة and خالة are both ___.","options":["cousin","aunt","uncle","grandma"],"answer":"aunt","explanation":"Think about the family tree: who is the parent of whom?","explanation_ar":"فكّر في شجرة العائلة."},{"q":"","options":["My Cousin is fahad.","My cousin is fahad.","my cousin is fahad.","My cousin is Fahad."],"answer":"My cousin is Fahad.","explanation":"Names of people start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"أسماء الأشخاص تبدأ بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["mrs. lama is our neighbor.","Mrs lama is our neighbor.","Mrs. Lama is our neighbor.","mrs. Lama is our neighbor"],"answer":"Mrs. Lama is our neighbor.","explanation":"Titles: Mr., Mrs., Ms., Dr. – capital letter and period.","explanation_ar":"الألقاب بحرف كبير ونقطة."},{"q":"Which words need capital letters? \"our dog is called rex.\"","options":["called, rex","is, our","dog, called","our, rex"],"answer":"our, rex","explanation":"A pet's name is a name: capital letter.","explanation_ar":"اسم الحيوان الأليف يبدأ بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["My dad is a Doctor.","my dad is a Doctor.","My Dad is a doctor.","My dad is a doctor."],"answer":"My dad is a doctor.","explanation":"After my/his/her, family words are small letters.","explanation_ar":"كلمات العائلة بعد my تُكتب صغيرة."},{"q":"Choose the best sentence for a family poster:","options":["My sister's name is Lama.","My sister name is Lama.","My sister her name is lama.","Name my sister is Lama."],"answer":"My sister's name is Lama.","explanation":"Add 's to the person to show who has the thing.","explanation_ar":"أضف 's للشخص لتدل على الملكية."},{"q":"How can we fix it? \"This is my uncle his name is Saad.\"","options":["This is my uncle, his name is saad.","This is my uncle. His name is Saad.","This is my uncle he name is Saad.","This my uncle. His name Saad."],"answer":"This is my uncle. His name is Saad.","explanation":"Names and titles start with a capital letter.","explanation_ar":"الأسماء والألقاب تبدأ بحرف كبير."},{"q":"My grandparents ___ in Abha.","options":["am","are","be","is"],"answer":"are","explanation":"Use am, is or are to match the subject.","explanation_ar":"استخدم am أو is أو are حسب الفاعل."},{"q":"Is this your pen? – No, it isn't. It's ___.","options":["Ali's","Ali his","Ali","Alis"],"answer":"Ali's","explanation":"Add 's to the person to show who has the thing.","explanation_ar":"أضف 's للشخص لتدل على الملكية."}],"theme_ar":"عائلتي","essential_question_ar":"مَن هم أفراد عائلتي، وما الذي يميّزهم؟","can_do":"I can talk about my family and say who things belong to with my, your, his, her and 's.","can_do_ar":"أستطيع أن أتحدث عن عائلتي وأقول لمن تعود الأشياء باستخدام my وyour وhis وher و's."});
